{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And the people heard this evil word.</b> It seems to me that Israel accepted upon themselves kinds of affliction, measure for measure: for at first their crowns were upon their heads and everlasting joy upon their head, and now when they heard of the withdrawal of the Shekhinah the joy withdrew, and therefore <b>they mourned.</b> And as for what it says <b>and did not put on,</b> since they were stripped of the glory of the Shekhinah that hovered over them, they stripped themselves of their ornaments — for we find that Scripture likened the departure of the Shekhinah to the stripping off of a garment, as Hosea said (Hosea 2:5) ״פן אפשיטנה ערומה והצגתיה כיום הולדה״ — that is, lest I strip from Israel the glory of My Shekhinah in which they were clothed, and they remain stripped of it as they were before the Torah was given, which is כיום הולדה; and so Targum Yonatan rendered: דלמא אסלק שכינתי מינה ואעדי יקרה ואשוינא רטישא כיומא קדמאה עד לא אתקרבת לפולחני."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:06:38.513345506Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}